[{:db/id 17592186129271 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0fc3f590-a25e-51e5-80e8-0d05b569e022" "question-03a9f960-3754-59ca-a7ce-a0ebf6a90fdf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129270 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b50230b8-d517-560a-9ede-747bedde3c3c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129269 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fa96e0b4-9142-5b9e-b173-68571a2c2de3" "question-bbf87425-cede-5e7e-870f-278bd2b11904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0fc3f590-a25e-51e5-80e8-0d05b569e022" :question/id #uuid "0fc3f590-a25e-51e5-80e8-0d05b569e022" :question/math-academy-id "q-39664" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=au,\\,y=bv,\\,z=cw.\n$$\n\nYou may assume that $a$, $b$ and $c$ are fixed constants." :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =a & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =b & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =a(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =a(bc-0) \\\\  & =abc.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3708f8e2-7d98-51bd-8b21-20ee27c9855a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3708f8e2-7d98-51bd-8b21-20ee27c9855a" :answer-field/id #uuid "3708f8e2-7d98-51bd-8b21-20ee27c9855a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434" :answer-field/choices ["answer-146610e3-5c1c-5561-9ca3-9774666c6c05" "answer-4d3fd2ac-fcea-50a9-92dd-45cccffc9e3a" "answer-b5179334-ac94-5f42-8f5c-8c9ece45c7a9" "answer-5938eea0-a7c5-5a7f-bf1f-a9fd0efaaf3a" "answer-7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-146610e3-5c1c-5561-9ca3-9774666c6c05" :answer/id #uuid "146610e3-5c1c-5561-9ca3-9774666c6c05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-a-b-c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d3fd2ac-fcea-50a9-92dd-45cccffc9e3a" :answer/id #uuid "4d3fd2ac-fcea-50a9-92dd-45cccffc9e3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-abc" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5179334-ac94-5f42-8f5c-8c9ece45c7a9" :answer/id #uuid "b5179334-ac94-5f42-8f5c-8c9ece45c7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5938eea0-a7c5-5a7f-bf1f-a9fd0efaaf3a" :answer/id #uuid "5938eea0-a7c5-5a7f-bf1f-a9fd0efaaf3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a+b+c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434" :answer/id #uuid "7a38c64c-896b-5232-a5e4-465265d40434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "abc" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-03a9f960-3754-59ca-a7ce-a0ebf6a90fdf" :question/id #uuid "03a9f960-3754-59ca-a7ce-a0ebf6a90fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-39294" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T$ that maps the $uvw$-space into the $xyz$-space by means of the equations\n\n$$\nx=v+w,\\,y=u+w,\\,z=u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)(0-1)+(1-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d447ea2-8560-5077-b8b9-f3304d7a91d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d447ea2-8560-5077-b8b9-f3304d7a91d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d447ea2-8560-5077-b8b9-f3304d7a91d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9406cdae-72e2-5c66-8ad2-f1e16969ae1d" "answer-af88273c-a488-5b6d-af48-680f8f2c6cda" "answer-6f2a26b3-3177-579e-877d-0fe20ffae536" "answer-de9aadb1-15c7-5202-b107-ef067be5cce6" "answer-09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9406cdae-72e2-5c66-8ad2-f1e16969ae1d" :answer/id #uuid "9406cdae-72e2-5c66-8ad2-f1e16969ae1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af88273c-a488-5b6d-af48-680f8f2c6cda" :answer/id #uuid "af88273c-a488-5b6d-af48-680f8f2c6cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f2a26b3-3177-579e-877d-0fe20ffae536" :answer/id #uuid "6f2a26b3-3177-579e-877d-0fe20ffae536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de9aadb1-15c7-5202-b107-ef067be5cce6" :answer/id #uuid "de9aadb1-15c7-5202-b107-ef067be5cce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862" :answer/id #uuid "09c7d7c2-430d-5af8-9d05-fa5665e62862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b50230b8-d517-560a-9ede-747bedde3c3c" :question/id #uuid "b50230b8-d517-560a-9ede-747bedde3c3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161811" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u}+v \\\\ v+w \\\\ vw\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={e}^{u}+v,\\,y(u,v,w)=v+w,\\,z(u,v,w)=vw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & w & v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ w & v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}(v-w).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{u}(v-w) & =0 \\\\ v-w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v-w=0$ defines the plane $v=w.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d0a37030-5cd9-5e43-a291-e19dfc94c67f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d0a37030-5cd9-5e43-a291-e19dfc94c67f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a37030-5cd9-5e43-a291-e19dfc94c67f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7447254c-742a-5c7f-adb1-193a3168832a" "answer-56201c08-96c0-58d8-9ed7-c9a2a6ecea11" "answer-2e37282e-8869-5ad2-9f01-e062a7d21846" "answer-4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" "answer-7473d403-04c8-5521-92cd-20ba6d10f904"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7447254c-742a-5c7f-adb1-193a3168832a" :answer/id #uuid "7447254c-742a-5c7f-adb1-193a3168832a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56201c08-96c0-58d8-9ed7-c9a2a6ecea11" :answer/id #uuid "56201c08-96c0-58d8-9ed7-c9a2a6ecea11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e37282e-8869-5ad2-9f01-e062a7d21846" :answer/id #uuid "2e37282e-8869-5ad2-9f01-e062a7d21846" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v=2{w}^{2}.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" :answer/id #uuid "4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=w.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7473d403-04c8-5521-92cd-20ba6d10f904" :answer/id #uuid "7473d403-04c8-5521-92cd-20ba6d10f904" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa96e0b4-9142-5b9e-b173-68571a2c2de3" :question/id #uuid "fa96e0b4-9142-5b9e-b173-68571a2c2de3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161797" :question/problem "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)),$ given that \n\n$$\nu=x,\\,v=2y,\\,w=3z.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9faf9fb-252c-510a-b14d-4675e0404650"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9faf9fb-252c-510a-b14d-4675e0404650" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9faf9fb-252c-510a-b14d-4675e0404650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d83940ba-986b-5a11-adf3-d93e8cc8e5b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f587a66a-7aeb-56f0-8880-52bcb09867b3" "answer-274585a0-b8c0-5396-9ba1-f844d74ca493" "answer-0584ff70-04f9-53f4-b918-d40c95661794" "answer-2dad3fa0-8b4c-595d-a450-31167f619d29" "answer-d83940ba-986b-5a11-adf3-d93e8cc8e5b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f587a66a-7aeb-56f0-8880-52bcb09867b3" :answer/id #uuid "f587a66a-7aeb-56f0-8880-52bcb09867b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-274585a0-b8c0-5396-9ba1-f844d74ca493" :answer/id #uuid "274585a0-b8c0-5396-9ba1-f844d74ca493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0584ff70-04f9-53f4-b918-d40c95661794" :answer/id #uuid "0584ff70-04f9-53f4-b918-d40c95661794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2dad3fa0-8b4c-595d-a450-31167f619d29" :answer/id #uuid "2dad3fa0-8b4c-595d-a450-31167f619d29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d83940ba-986b-5a11-adf3-d93e8cc8e5b6" :answer/id #uuid "d83940ba-986b-5a11-adf3-d93e8cc8e5b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bbf87425-cede-5e7e-870f-278bd2b11904" :question/id #uuid "bbf87425-cede-5e7e-870f-278bd2b11904" :question/math-academy-id "q-161808" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y,z)\\to (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{y} \\\\ y \\\\ xz\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$\n\n*Hint: You can assume that $y,z\\ne 0.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nu(x,y,z)=\\frac{z}{y},\\,v(x,y,z)=y,\\,w(x,y,z)=xz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =-\\frac{z}{{y}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =z & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{z}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ z & 0 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =z|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =z(0-\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{z}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting down $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}$ in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z}{y} & =-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-u)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f602c505-c9b2-58a6-873a-3101dc02439a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f602c505-c9b2-58a6-873a-3101dc02439a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f602c505-c9b2-58a6-873a-3101dc02439a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba467583-3a17-5baa-8344-2ff452a1d080" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba467583-3a17-5baa-8344-2ff452a1d080" "answer-fa885cf6-9f29-528c-8aeb-86e960fc0083" "answer-ecf34300-0330-5f0e-9e12-24a74c4b83db" "answer-bc7a65b8-5911-5995-890e-26eb26de2d86" "answer-cda476b6-e024-5c13-a813-a0217e4446ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba467583-3a17-5baa-8344-2ff452a1d080" :answer/id #uuid "ba467583-3a17-5baa-8344-2ff452a1d080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa885cf6-9f29-528c-8aeb-86e960fc0083" :answer/id #uuid "fa885cf6-9f29-528c-8aeb-86e960fc0083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{w}{v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecf34300-0330-5f0e-9e12-24a74c4b83db" :answer/id #uuid "ecf34300-0330-5f0e-9e12-24a74c4b83db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2u}{v-w}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc7a65b8-5911-5995-890e-26eb26de2d86" :answer/id #uuid "bc7a65b8-5911-5995-890e-26eb26de2d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{vw}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cda476b6-e024-5c13-a813-a0217e4446ba" :answer/id #uuid "cda476b6-e024-5c13-a813-a0217e4446ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
